  "design": "Fact questions only, from validation initial_packet cases outside S. The other cases are shuffled with random.Random(3) and taken in that order until 128 fact questions, then frozen before any call. Names are {row_id}::fact::{fact}. A call's state is {packets: [{case_id, state: case.state()}]} for exactly the cases named by that call's questions. Every batch question, including the one-case call, uses the same pre-registered prefix that names the case_id, then the standard fact instructions, so question count is the factor that changes. Drex is called three times: the first other case's fact questions, the first 32 frozen questions, and the first 128. GPT is called twice: the first 8 and the first 16 of that same list. GPT is not sent the one-case, 32-question, or 128-question cells. Invalid means a call error, a missing choice, a choice outside the options, or the frontier adapter's raw error for an invalid or missing choice. Invalid rows stay in the accuracy denominator and count as incorrect.",
  "caveats": [
    "Validation initial_packet only. The development 370-case panel and the development parquet were not read.",
    "Option order was not shuffled. That cell was skipped so the GPT request count stays at or under 24.",
    "These n are a pilot. A Wilson interval at this size is wide, including when the point estimate is 0 or 1.",
    "Criteria-gym records often say explicitly whether a clause is satisfied, so a small or empty gap is a real result.",
    "The injected note and the paraphrase were fixed before any model call and were not rewritten after the results.",
    "GPT latency_ms includes shared rate-limit wait (FRONTIER_RPM stays at the default). service_latency_ms subtracts that wait.",
    "Frontier case_id is sent beside state by the existing adapter. Drex's request has no case_id field. The state and the questions are the shared input.",
    "Costs use the adapter's billed figures (configured router rates and Drex input-token price).",
    "GPT cells at one_case, q32, and q128 were not run. The missing 128-question GPT cell is by design.",
    "Invalid rows are counted in the accuracy denominator. invalid_rate is the share that a drop rule would have removed.",
    "The batch state is a packet list, including the one-case call, so it is not the same prompt as the inject arm.",
    "Paired GPT numbers at 8 and 16 reuse Drex answers from the larger packed call when that call contains the same question names."
  ],
